      "body": "## Motivation\n\nSame loss pattern as #41909 / #41914 / #41962: `PythonicDetector`,\n`InklingDetector`, `Gemma4Detector` and `PoolsideV1Detector` hold text back\nin `self._buffer` while waiting for the closing tool-call marker (or a\nmatching bracket / tag). `BaseFormatDetector.finish()` returns an empty\nresult by default, so when the stream ends with an incomplete marker still\nbuffered, the held-back text is silently dropped:\n\n```python\nd = PythonicDetector()\nd.parse_streaming_increment(\"hi [get_weather(city=\", [])\nd.finish([])  # returns empty; \"[get_weather(city=\" is lost\n```\n\n## Changes\n\nAdd a `finish()` override to each detector that flushes `_buffer` as normal\ntext, matching the existing pattern in `IQuestQ1Detector.finish` and the\nfixes in #41909 / #41914 / #41962. Normal streams are unaffected:\n`finish()` stays a no-op when `_buffer` is empty.\n\n## Tests\n\nOffline unit tests (no server, no model loading) for each detector cover:\n- partial tool call at stream end: `finish()` releases the buffered text;\n- clean stream: `finish()` returns an empty result;\n- fully parsed stream: no duplication at `finish()`.\n\nAll pass locally (`pytest test/registered/unit/function_call/test_{pythonic,inkling,gemma4,poolside_v1}_detector_finish.py`), ruff clean.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37403226036](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37403226036)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37403225581](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37403225581)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37403226100](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37403226100)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
      "changedFiles": 8,
